cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DICOM-Atlas: An open registry of public and private DICOM tags"
message: >
  If you use DICOM-Atlas in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Citation is encouraged and appreciated but not legally required.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Riley
    given-names: Nathan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1579-7312"
    website: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/DICOM-Atlas"
url: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/DICOM-Atlas"
abstract: >
  DICOM-Atlas is an open registry of public and private DICOM tags compiled
  from vendor conformance statements (GE HealthCare, Siemens Healthineers,
  Philips Healthcare) and the DICOM PS3.6 standard. Each tag record includes
  the value representation (VR), value multiplicity (VM), human-readable name,
  private creator string, and source citations back to the originating
  conformance document page. The registry is distributed as a human-editable
  CSV (tags.csv), a memory-mapped binary (tags.dmap), and queryable via
  a Rust library, Python bindings, and C FFI.
license: "Apache-2.0"
date-released: "2026-05-31"
version: "0.2.6"
keywords:
  - DICOM
  - medical imaging
  - private tags
  - radiology
  - data dictionary
  - interoperability
  - conformance statements
  - GE HealthCare
  - Siemens Healthineers
  - Philips Healthcare
